{"Admin group pagination computes totalPages using Math.floor(user_count/limit)+1, which overcounts when user_count is exactly divisible by limit, enabling navigation to a non-existent extra page and requests with offset == user_count that return empty member lists": 0.9098326563835144, "The public group members template iterates 'members', but the group-members route only sets 'model' and never sets a 'members' property on the controller, so the template has no bound list to render and can show an empty table even though findMembers() populates model.members": 0.8950321078300476, "Discourse.Group.findMembers() fetches a paginated member list with a default limit of 50, but the public group members page has no pagination controls or load-more behavior, so groups with more than 50 members cannot be fully browsed from the public UI": 0.9540031552314758, "Admin::GroupsController#remove_member removes the GroupUser join row but does not clear users.primary_group_id when it points at the removed group, leaving users referencing a primary group they are no longer a member of": 0.689545750617981}